WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.960
Can you let go of my hand first?

2
00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.420
Seulgi, today is your first time coming to our school

3
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.380
Please hold my hand well and don't get lost

4
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.790
Xiaojing, you are smarter
Come and analyze it

5
00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.740
what is going on

6
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.030
who knows

7
00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.990
By the way, I haven't introduced myself yet, have I?

8
00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:51.990
My name is Zhu Yili and you?

9
00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:53.930
My name is Yu Seqi

10
00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:55.600
My name is Cui Jing

11
00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.749
Thinking about it carefully, I seem to have never
Never told anyone my name

12
00:01:00.749 --> 00:01:02.800
Seulgi, today is your first time coming to our school

13
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.150
Please hold my hand well and don't get lost

14
00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:07.190
Seulgi, why did you transfer here?

15
00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.050
Few people transfer schools during their senior year of high school

16
00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.910
I transferred here because of my parents

17
00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:14.610
What do your parents do?

18
00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:15.969
Are they transferring here?

19
00:01:15.969 --> 00:01:17.480
Not that case…

20
00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.120
where did you live before

21
00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:21.340
Even if I say it, you may not have heard it.

22
00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:23.810
Because it’s a small place in the countryside

23
00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.920
I'm from other places too
Live alone now

24
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.780
Live in a big house of 60 square meters
There are also maids to help with cleaning

25
00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:28.689
Can I live here by myself?

26
00:01:28.689 --> 00:01:32.270
Do you know what it feels like to live apart from your parents?

27
00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:34.360
Xiaojing probably rarely sees her parents.

28
00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.520
Because they have many cases

29
00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.450
right

30
00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:37.990
That's right

31
00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.870
Your mother is a lawyer and your father is a prosecutor.

32
00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:41.890
Why didn't you want to study law?

33
00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:43.000
What does it have to do with you

34
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.280
Jai also wanted to inherit her father’s hospital
I just want to get admitted to the Department of Medicine at a Korean University

35
00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.410
Did your parents graduate from the music department?

36
00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:50.390
No

37
00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:53.470
I'm here to complete my mother
Unfulfilled artistic dream

38
00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:57.320
Have you heard that harps are the most expensive?
You should choose the one with the lowest competition rate, right?

39
00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:57.930
Hello

40
00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.789
Seulgi, do you also want to get admitted to a Korean university?

41
00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.170
Generally, everyone will place the area around the target university
Take it with you

42
00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:08.420
like a talisman

43
00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:13.580
I am also collecting peripherals from Korean universities.

44
00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:16.740
But that keychain of yours is a limited edition
hard to buy

45
00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:23.110
Do you really want to get admitted to a Korean university?

46
00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.180
What major do you want to take?

47
00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.020
That…

48
00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.510
I also want to take the medical exam

49
00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:36.690
So you are going to live and study
Did you just check out today?

50
00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.680
Did you ask for a tutor? Who did you learn from?

51
00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.180
I didn't ask for a tutor

52
00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.440
What? Didn’t you hire a tutor?

53
00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:43.130
What about cram school?

54
00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:44.780
Which cram school do you go to?

55
00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:46.890
I didn’t go to cram school either

56
00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.400
What a rare species

57
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:53.010
Jay next to you
Bao Zhun attended the medical department of a Korean university

58
00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:55.150
I hired three math tutors

59
00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.590
Xiaojing, please stop talking.

60
00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.600
No, because she is too outrageous

61
00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.490
I didn’t take any tutoring at all and wanted to get into a Korean university.

62
00:03:01.039 --> 00:03:04.330
I still want to take the medical exam. Isn’t it too naive?

63
00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:10.160
Aren’t there solutions and answers in the exercise book?

64
00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:12.600
did you hear what she said

65
00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.520
Are you too naive or too ignorant?

66
00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.280
I'm asking because I really don't understand.

67
00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.000
That's right, Seulgi, you're right
It’s all in the exercise book

68
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.010
But the same question can have different solutions

69
00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:26.100
Learn different solutions from different teachers
It's beneficial and harmless

70
00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:29.810
Senior sister

71
00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.340
Thank you. I'm not welcome then.

72
00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:50.770
What medicines have you taken recently?
Can't recover strength

73
00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:52.540
Then quit smoking

74
00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.600
Do you want to get an IV drip?

75
00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.660
I can make an appointment for you

76
00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.799
Jay’s father’s dripping regimen is indeed very effective

77
00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:00.590
Seulgi, do you want to come with me?

78
00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.680
My dad will help everyone take care of themselves

79
00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.790
If you want to study well, you must have good physical strength

80
00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:08.120
thank you for your kindness

81
00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.050
but i don't need

82
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.480
ok

83
00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:12.890
Then tell me when you need it

84
00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.210
what are you doing

85
00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.670
I want to change seats

86
00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.450
Her name is Jin Nali or Cui Nali?

87
00:04:56.450 --> 00:04:58.410
Anyway, I told her to change seats.

88
00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.890
Did Jay agree?

89
00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:02.240
I want to change seats

90
00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:03.660
Do I need her to agree?

91
00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.710
Why should I trust you? Drink your water

92
00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:55.040
Who knows what you added to the water?

93
00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:58.000
what are you talking about

94
00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.230
I didn't add anything to the water

95
00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:00.160
I just think you swallow the medicine dryly like this...

96
00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:04.150
You must feel now
I'm a lunatic with persecutory delusions.

97
00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:05.680
But you'll know after a while

98
00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.200
Since he was selected by Liu Jieyi

99
00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.590
You won't last long

100
00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:28.600
what on earth are you thinking

101
00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:31.760
You don't plan on taking that country bumpkin with you all the time, do you?

102
00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:41.260
Take it away quickly. I hate mice so much.

103
00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:42.600
Don't you think it's cute?

104
00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:58.330
I object to letting people of unknown origin join us

105
00:06:58.330 --> 00:06:59.350
Really?

106
00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.190
So what if you object?

107
00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.140
[Korean University Admissions Brochure]

108
00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.040
This year’s admissions requirements
Being a class leader gets extra points

109
00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.700
How about you? Do you want to be the monitor of the first semester?

110
00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.500
[Extra 10% points for class leaders]

111
00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.560
are you serious

112
00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.790
Of course

113
00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:26.150
Don't go back on your word

114
00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:40.860
[Caihua]

115
00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:44.340
[Second-hand items buying and selling
watercolor palette watercolor paint]

116
00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:51.340
[Zhengcaihua Girls' High School Uniform]

117
00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:54.360
Seulgi, why are you sitting here?

118
00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:55.920
Because…

119
00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:59.770
My eyesight is not very good and I can’t see the blackboard clearly.

120
00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:02.120
Then why didn't you tell me earlier?
We can change seats together

121
00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:03.720
good wisdom

122
00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:05.350
OK…

123
00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:08.710
It would be better if you don't bother others.

124
00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:20.160
Since you think so

125
00:08:20.869 --> 00:08:22.040
ok

126
00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:33.610
Jay, are you unhappy?

127
00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.350
Of course not

128
00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:36.210
Please give me more advice in the future

129
00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:37.580
Don't say that

130
00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:38.640
How can I be that powerful?

131
00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.920
I've always wanted to sit next to you

132
00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.770
I didn’t expect that this wish would not come true until my senior year of high school.

133
00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:44.860
It seems that I can get into a good university with you.

134
00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:47.000
Please teach me more in the future

135
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.410
There is nothing to teach or not to teach

136
00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.690
We are friends

137
00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:53.000
For the first time, my grades are like yours
Such nice people sitting together

138
00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.680
really nervous

139
00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:58.520
It's also my first time

140
00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:00.080
Sitting with people I didn't choose

141
00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.120
The phone you dialed is not turned on

142
00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:14.360
Will be forwarded to voicemail

143
00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.210
Charges will start after the beep

144
00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:31.530
Hello

145
00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:35.240
How are you doing lately?

146
00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:37.720
School starts today

147
00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:50.530
Ah, right

148
00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:55.760
You have it among your father's belongings
Do you see the mobile phone?

149
00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:59.410
Well, I didn't see this

150
00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.680
It's a Galaxy phone, not the latest model.

151
00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:05.470
You know, studied at a Korean university
The cell phone on the keychain

152
00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:06.890
Did you really not see it?

153
00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:08.610
No

154
00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:10.990
sorry

155
00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:14.890
It's not your fault

156
00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:44.140
[May the deceased rest in peace]

157
00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.300
After she disappeared

158
00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:38.990
Her mother died not long after, didn't she?

159
00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:43.180
Why are you still looking for her?

160
00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.030
She is not your biological child

161
00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:48.790
Do you want to take her back to live with you?

162
00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:11.900
[Searching for missing children Yu Seulqi]

163
00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:09.660
[Seller: Do you want to buy the uniform of Caihua Girls High School]

164
00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:13.820
[Yu Seqi: Yes, can we meet in person today?]

165
00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:16.980
[At about 10 p.m. at Yeoksam Station Exit 8]

166
00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:27.740
[Seller: Have you arrived at Exit 8]

167
00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.580
[Arrived. Where are you?]

168
00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.860
[Yiksam Station Exit 8]

169
00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:35.300
[Seller: Go straight after exiting]

170
00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:41.620
[Seller: Go straight to the first alley and turn left
Then continue straight]

171
00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:53.420
[Seller: Almost there, go a little further]

172
00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:05.280
[Seller: I saw a golden billboard
Does it say Erato Hotel? Please wait there]

173
00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.080
Are you here to buy uniforms?

174
00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:15.770
Yes

175
00:13:48.980 --> 00:13:50.740
[Unknown caller]

176
00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:30.820
Good morning, teacher

177
00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:31.810
early

178
00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:02.280
What should I do? My hand slipped accidentally

179
00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:07.760
It doesn't matter

180
00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:09.530
Just wash it

181
00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:12.090
I feel so sorry

182
00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:13.750
How should I compensate you?

183
00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:15.620
It really doesn't matter

184
00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:21.470
But are you sure this thing can really be washed off?

185
00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:26.510
That's right too

186
00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:28.340
You are so tolerant

187
00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:30.920
Even if it gets dirty
You probably won't care either, right?

188
00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:34.710
Don’t you understand yet?

189
00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:38.050
Your uniform reeks of semen.

190
00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:43.220
Jai, be nice to you

191
00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:45.460
Do you really think you have become Cinderella?

192
00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:57.990
So disgusting

193
00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:01.600
-It's too dirty
-what to do

194
00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:06.060
-Oh my god
-So disgusting...

195
00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:11.520
what to do

196
00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:17.390
Hello

197
00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:22.430
go away…

198
00:16:22.430 --> 00:16:24.320
Damn it

199
00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:25.890
Seulgi

200
00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:27.410
How long has it been since you changed your sanitary napkin?

201
00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:29.950
Do you know how strong the smell of blood is on you?

202
00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:32.130
There are no insoles in your shoes, right?

203
00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:34.340
Do you use sanitary napkins as insoles?

204
00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.490
Take it off and see...

205
00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:37.610
so funny

206
00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:42.270
Come on Seulgi

207
00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.350
take off

208
00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:56.029
you bitch

209
00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:49.280
Seulgi

210
00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:01.500
You can just fit into my arms

211
00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.910
We seem to be about the same size

212
00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:10.080
I hate getting dirty things on my clothes.

213
00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:12.220
So I always keep a few extra items in my locker for backup.

214
00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:13.730
Let me wear this one for you

215
00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.260
No thanks for your kindness

216
00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:17.280
That dress can't be worn anymore

217
00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:18.600
You'd better wear this one

218
00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:19.050
Do you want me to change it for you?

219
00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:20.460
I said no need

220
00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:22.320
I'm different from you

221
00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:25.350
Even if the clothes are dirty and smelly
I can still wear it

222
00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:27.900
I don't even care anymore. Why are you meddling in your own business?

223
00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:31.660
You don't know what "reject" means, right?

224
00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:34.000
Make no mistake

225
00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:36.360
Not everyone is willing to accept your kindness

226
00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:39.040
ok

227
00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:41.310
I know, stop talking

228
00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:08.640
Let’s take a look at the problem-solving speed during winter vacation training
Have you made any progress?

229
00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:11.130
Give you 20 minutes

230
00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:13.620
start

231
00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.690
We haven't learned these yet, right?

232
00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:34.050
Why doesn't anyone find it strange?

233
00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:37.810
Am I the only one who hasn't learned it yet?
Everyone has learned it, right?

234
00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:59.230
You should write at least the seventh question during this time.

235
00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:14.460
Okay, stop moving

236
00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:15.780
put down the pen

237
00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.680
The students in the last row began to collect papers

238
00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:38.620
Liu Jieyi 10 points

239
00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.160
Cui Jing 9 points

240
00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:43.590
Kim Bum-soo 8 points

241
00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:46.210
Zhao Yaluo 8 points

242
00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:47.780
Goo Chae Ryung 7 points

243
00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:49.070
Li Shiyu 6 points

244
00:20:49.070 --> 00:20:50.450
Jin Nali 6 points

245
00:20:50.450 --> 00:20:52.200
Park Byung-hee 6 points

246
00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:54.820
There’s no need to study for lower scores, right?

247
00:20:58.350 --> 00:20:59.660
After class

248
00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:07.970
Why doesn't the tutor answer the phone?
I'm going crazy

249
00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:12.720
Please Jay, tell us the answer
It's faster

250
00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:14.020
Jay, what’s the answer to question 2?

251
00:21:14.020 --> 00:21:14.940
And question 5

252
00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:15.670
What about question 7?

253
00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:16.650
What about question 8?

254
00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:19.360
I will start with the answer from question 1
Read them all again

255
00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:20.570
Good

256
00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:26.250
a equals 5

257
00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:29.370
The answer to question 2 is -3

258
00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:31.450
teacher

259
00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:34.320
What's wrong

260
00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:40.150
Can I ask my score?

261
00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:45.560
Yu Seqi

262
00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:46.640
4 points

263
00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:50.620
I heard that you were number one in your previous school.

264
00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:51.620
I was still looking forward to it

265
00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:53.160
The result is really disappointing

266
00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:56.590
As expected, the level of rural schools
It can't be compared with our school, right?

267
00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:58.380
teacher

